# Normalize the line endings in the working tree.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) makes a
# checkout write CRLF while the files that were already in the tree used LF.
# The two spellings are indistinguishable to git but not to the test suite:
# several source-contract assertions compare multi-line string literals
# against the raw file content, and a CRLF checkout made them fail even
# though nothing about the code had changed.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's binary detection, so the favicon and the generated
# bundles are still stored byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf
